\section{The reported mean is not written anywhere}{

For functional coding the implied mean of the \strong{genetic component} is
\verb{mu = a(p - q) + 2pq*d}. It is reported and stored nowhere — in particular
not in \code{phenotype_meta.mean}, which would double-count it once non-additive
genetic values reach the phenotype layer, because the raw genetic values
already have expectation \code{mu}. The running total across loci is reported only
because every term here is a single-locus main effect; no such total exists
for an epistatic term, whose expectation depends on joint genotype
frequencies and LD.
